/-! ## The INIT alone does not separate symmetric inputs

bd_c2n is maj(a, ~b, q) with a and q symmetric: on ce_pair seed 4 the map
with feedback and request SWAPPED also realizes the INIT. So the `_src` facts
(which net the active pips connect) are what put the feedback on B1 there. -/
theorem c2n_init_symmetric :
    Realizes Formal.Net.Fasm.CePairS4.lut0 .o6 (o6B initC2n) vec4 [0, 2, 4, 3] 4 = true ∧
    Realizes Formal.Net.Fasm.CePairS4.lut0 .o6 (o6B initC2n) vec4 [4, 2, 0, 3] 4 = true := by
  decide

/-- Negative control: a wrong map (ack and feedback swapped) does NOT realize
the INIT, so `Realizes` can fail. -/
theorem wrong_map_fails :
    Realizes Formal.Net.Fasm.CePairS4.lut0 .o6 (o6B initC2n) vec4 [4, 0, 2, 3] 4 = false := by
  decide

end Formal.Cells.PinAssign
